# Chromium's extension install prompt wants a Chromium browser window to hang from as a sheet: the
# page's top-level window. Cra embeds pages in its own window, so the prompt got none and Chromium
# showed it free-standing: placed against the screen, unmovable, with macOS's title bar over the
# prompt's title (GitHub #349). It must hang over Cra's window, on the screen, clear of the title bar.
# A made-up store page (web-store.html, on the address --apps-gallery-url names) asks for the
# install the way the Web Store's own page does.
# promise: #349
budget rss=600
arg --apps-gallery-url=${ORIGIN}/
cra://open?url=${ORIGIN}/web-store.html
wait 3
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"ask()","userGesture":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*asked
expect-log Chromium dialog [0-9]+ shown over window
cra://debug?chromiumDialogs=1
expect-log Chromium dialogs: frame=\{\{.*\}\} over=\{\{.*\}\} onScreen=true titleBarHidden=true
reject-log over=none
